真不敢相信我竟然错过了。

314
00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:07.340
I thought it was brilliant.
我觉得这太天才了。

315
00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:09.020
I love this little piece of detail.
我喜欢这个小细节。

316
00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:13.720
Well, Dwight's going to wake up Kathy by yelling in her ear and scaring her.
嗯，德怀特打算在凯西耳边大喊大叫，把她吓醒。

317
00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:18.380
Then he tries to do the same thing to Aaron, but Aaron is sleeping with her feet on her pillow
然后他想对艾伦如法炮制，但艾伦睡觉时脚放在枕头上，

318
00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:19.600
and whacks him in the head.
直接给了他脑袋一下。

319
00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:25.280
Then they try to wake up Stanley, because now Aaron's helping him, but Stanley won't
接着他们去叫醒斯坦利，因为现在艾伦在帮他，但斯坦利就是不肯

320
00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:28.120
wake up, so Dwight basically holds his nose and closes his mouth.
醒来，所以德怀特干脆捏住他的鼻子，闭上他的嘴。

321
00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:29.240
That is terrifying.
那太可怕了。

322
00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:30.860
Can you imagine waking up like that?
你能想象那样醒来吗？

323
00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:31.340
I cannot.
我无法想象。

324
00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:36.980
Then they go in to wake up Ryan, and Aaron kind of is like, hey, you want to wake up?
然后他们去叫醒瑞安，艾伦大概是说，嘿，你想醒过来吗？

325
00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:38.340
Ryan is so excited.
瑞安非常兴奋。

326
00:13:38.620 --> 00:13:41.720
Apparently, he went to her door twice the night before.
显然，前一天晚上他去过她房间两次。

327
00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:42.540
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

328
00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:46.340
Then he realizes it's just Dwight trying to wake him up, and he's like, not cool.
然后他意识到只是德怀特在叫他起床，他觉得这很不酷。

329
00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:51.280
Last person they go to wake up is Jim, but Jim's been up for a long time.
他们去叫醒的最后一个人是吉姆，但吉姆早就醒了。

330
00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:53.180
He's on a two-kids sleep schedule.
他现在是两个孩子的作息时间。

331
00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:56.980
I would like to play a bullshit card real quick.
我想快速打出一张“胡扯”牌。

332
00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:57.380
Okay.
好的。

333
00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:04.500
In Dwight's talking head, he says that Jim takes 50 minutes to style his hair.
在德怀特的访谈里，他说吉姆做发型要花50分钟。

334
00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:05.260
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

335
00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:07.540
Shouldn't he have woken Jim up first?
那他不应该先去叫醒吉姆吗？

336
00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:12.180
According to his talking head, Jim needs the most time in the morning.
根据他的访谈，吉姆早上最需要时间。

337
00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:15.220
Why is he the last room they go to, Dwight?
德怀特，为什么他是你们最后去的房间？

338
00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:16.920
I accept your bullshit card.
我接受你的“胡扯”牌。

339
00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:17.420
Thank you.
谢谢。

340
00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:22.300
I was curious about this scene, you know, Jim's elaborate prank of how he's trying
我对这一幕很好奇，你知道的，吉姆那个精心设计的恶作剧，他试图

341
00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:24.680
to fake his own death, and they walk into the room.
伪造自己的死亡，然后他们走进房间。

342
00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:26.300
Yes, and frame Dwight for it.
没错，还要嫁祸给德怀特。

343
00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:26.960
Exactly.
正是如此。

344
00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:29.740
I was curious how it was described in the script.
我很好奇剧本里是怎么描述这一幕的。

345
00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:30.760
This is what it said.
剧本上是这么写的。

346
00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:35.920
Camera turns to reveal that Jim has set up the room to look like an insane crime scene.
镜头转过去，揭示了吉姆把房间布置得像个疯狂的犯罪现场。

347
00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:41.720
There's an open briefcase with money spilling out of it, a blood-soaked towel in the corner,
有一个打开的公文包，钱散落出来，角落里有一条浸满血的毛巾，

348
00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:45.720
the mattress is overturned, the TV is set to static,
床垫被掀翻了，电视机调到了雪花屏，

349
00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:51.680
the balcony door is open, there are sheets tied into a rope going over the balcony's edge.
阳台门开着，床单系成的绳子从阳台边缘垂了下去。

350
00:14:51.860 --> 00:14:55.600
Now, here's something that I found really interesting about this scene,
现在，关于这一幕，我发现了一件非常有趣的事情，

351
00:14:55.780 --> 00:15:00.540
which is that in reality, when Dwight and Erin walk into the room,
那就是在现实中，当德怀特和艾琳走进房间时，

352
00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:06.440
they would have taken in all of these details probably at the same time.
他们很可能会同时注意到所有这些细节。

353
00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:11.180
For example, the sign on the wall that says Dwight did it.
比如墙上写着“德怀特干的”那个牌子。

354
00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:11.480
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

355
00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:21.100
They might have seen that first, but they wait to react until the camera has panned around the room
他们可能先看到了那个，但他们会等到镜头扫过整个房间，

356
00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:26.940
and ends on Dwight did it, and then they react to it, which I just thought was really interesting
最后停在“德怀特干的”那个牌子上时才做出反应，我觉得这真的很有趣，

357
00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:33.120
because we are assuming that they saw the room the way the camera saw the room.
因为我们假设他们看房间的方式和摄像机看房间的方式是一样的。

358
00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:36.060
But really, if you walk in a room, you see it all at once, right?
但实际上，如果你走进一个房间，你是同时看到所有东西的，对吧？

359
00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:36.520
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

360
00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:39.840
I just thought that was interesting storytelling maneuver.
我只是觉得这是一种有趣的叙事手法。

361
00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:42.660
I feel like you're calling bulls**t on a few things today.
我觉得你今天是在质疑一些事情。

362
00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:46.160
You're like, I call bulls**t on the camera work.
你就像是在说，我质疑这种摄像手法。

363
00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:53.440
No, it's just, I guess it would be like on the delayed reaction of Dwight and Erin.
不，只是，我想说的是德怀特和艾琳的反应延迟。

364
00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:56.180
I feel like they would have reacted much sooner,
我觉得他们本应该更早做出反应的，

365
00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:59.500
but they had to wait for the camera to get to the sign.
但他们必须等镜头移到那个牌子上。

366
00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:00.040
Exactly.
没错。

367
00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:05.320
Well, this whole cold open, Angela, took me down a road that is very random.
嗯，安吉拉，整个开场戏让我陷入了一个非常随机的思考中。

368
00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:13.980
I got curious about how early do you need to wake up in the morning before you can walk out the door?
我很好奇，出门前你需要提前多久起床？

369
00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:17.000
How long does the average person need in the morning?
普通人早上需要多长时间？

370
00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:22.280
And I actually found an article that was on Glamour Magazine's website,
我实际上在《魅力》杂志的网站上找到了一篇文章，

371
00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:28.020
and it broke down the average amount of time that both men and women need for grooming in the morning.
它详细分析了男女早上梳洗所需的平均时间。

372
00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:28.740
Oh, let's hear it.
哦，说来听听。

373
00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:29.920
Does this interest you?
你感兴趣吗？

374
00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:37.640
It does, because just this morning, I sort of shared that I am done maintaining the back of my head.
感兴趣，因为就在今天早上，我分享过我不再打理后脑勺了。

375
00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:38.900
Okay.
好吧。

376
00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:39.860
I'm done.
我放弃了。

377
00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:41.460
And how much time will this save you?
这能为你节省多少时间？

378
00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:45.400
I'm hoping quite a bit, because I have a cowlick in the back of my head,
我希望不少，因为我后脑勺有个发旋，

379
00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:48.420
and I have to back comb, and I have to hairspray.
我得倒梳，还得喷发胶。

380
00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:53.080
I have to, like, do things so the Red Sea doesn't part back there every day.
我得做各种处理，免得每天那里都像红海分界一样裂开。

381
00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:53.480
Right.
对。

382
00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:54.940
And I'm done.
我放弃了。

383
00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:55.700
I'm done.
我放弃了。

384
00:16:56.220 --> 00:16:56.920
You know what?
你知道吗？

385
00:16:56.920 --> 00:17:02.200
If you see me out and about, and you see the back of my head looking like a hot mess, just know that I'm done.
如果你在外面看到我，发现我的后脑勺乱七八糟的，就当我是故意的。

386
00:17:02.320 --> 00:17:02.980
It's intentional.
这是故意的。

387
00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:03.100
It's intentional.
这是故意的。

388
00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:03.720
I'm done.
我放弃了。

389
00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:04.400
Okay.
好吧。

390
00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:05.760
Good to know.
知道了。

391
00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:10.300
The back of my head looks quite wonky lately because of my shoulder, so we're quite a pair.
因为肩膀的原因，我后脑勺最近看起来挺怪的，所以我们俩真是绝配。

392
00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:12.560
That would be our paparazzi photo.
那会是我们的狗仔队照片。

393
00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:14.680
Like, no one's taking pictures of us.
就像，没人会拍我们。

394
00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:15.300
Like, who cares?
谁在乎呢？

395
00:17:15.460 --> 00:17:18.780
But what I'd love to see out there is just a photo of the back of our heads.
但我很想看到一张我们后脑勺的照片。

396
00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:20.620
Just looking horrible.
看起来糟糕透顶的那种。

397
00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:23.360
Ah, one can dream.
啊，做梦吧。

398
00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:27.440
Well, according to this article by Glamour Magazine,
嗯，根据《魅力》杂志的这篇文章，

399
00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:33.180
the average time that a woman spends on grooming in the morning is 22.5 minutes,
女性早上梳洗的平均时间是22.5分钟，

400
00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:35.660
and men average 20 minutes.
而男性平均是20分钟。

401
00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:42.360
However, they pointed to a study that said that the longer someone spends getting ready in the morning,
然而，他们指出一项研究表明，一个人早上准备的时间越长，

402
00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:45.720
the more likely they are to feel negative about their appearance.
就越容易对自己的外表感到消极。

403
00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:46.320
Oh.
噢。

404
00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:51.480
But the less time you spend grooming in the morning, the more positively they view their appearance.
但早上花在打扮上的时间越少，他们对自己的外表就看得越正面。

405
00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:53.200
And I was thinking about that.
我当时就在想这件事。

406
00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:54.520
I'm like, you know what?
我在想，你知道吗？

407
00:17:54.520 --> 00:18:01.060
I have to say it kind of makes sense to me because the more time I spend scrutinizing in front of a mirror,
我不得不说这对我来说有点道理，因为我在镜子前审视自己的时间越长，

408
00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:03.100
the less confident I feel.
我就越感到不自信。

409
00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:07.300
So I do kind of like to just get that morning routine over with.
所以我确实喜欢尽快搞定早上的例行公事。

410
00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:10.620
I think for me it changed as I aged, you know?
我觉得对我来说，随着年龄增长，情况发生了变化，你知道吗？

411
00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:14.920
Because here I am 52, and I'm like, I'm done taking care of the back of my head.
因为我都52岁了，我在想，我不想再管后脑勺的头发了。

412
00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:15.280
Right?
对吧？

413
00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:19.280
When I was younger, I spent more time trying to look nice.
我年轻的时候，花更多时间打扮自己。

414
00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:19.760
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

415
00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:20.200
Same.
我也是。

416
00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:21.600
And now I spend less time.
现在我花的时间少了。

417
00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:22.060
We've given up.
我们放弃了。

418
00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:23.160
I don't know.
我不知道。

419
00:18:23.340 --> 00:18:31.760
Well, I think for me in terms of grooming, I need 12 minutes to pull myself together, 20 if I'm trying hard.
嗯，我觉得就打扮而言，我需要12分钟来收拾自己，如果努力一点的话需要20分钟。

420
00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:36.360
But in general, as I get older, I like a real long runway in the morning.
但总的来说，随着年龄增长，我喜欢早上有很长的缓冲时间。

421
00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:39.300
I like to ease into my day slowly.
我喜欢慢慢地开始我的一天。

422
00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:48.360
So Dwight would need to wake me up like a good 90 minutes before he wants me to be like participating in a workday, I think.
所以我觉得德怀特得在我开始工作前至少提前90分钟叫醒我。

423
00:18:49.260 --> 00:18:49.380
Yeah.
是啊。

424
00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:51.720
Dwight doesn't want to come wake me up.
德怀特不想来叫醒我。

425
00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:53.780
He doesn't?
他不想吗？

426
00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:54.080
No.
不想。

427
00:18:54.560 --> 00:18:55.320
Oh, boy.
天哪。

428
00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:57.040
Don't come at me, Dwight.
别来找我，德怀特。

429
00:18:57.180 --> 00:18:57.840
Not in the morning.
别在早上。

430
00:18:57.840 --> 00:19:04.420
I do want to say the way that John as Jim fell out of the closet, I thought was so good.
我得说，约翰饰演的吉姆从壁橱里摔出来的方式，我觉得太棒了。

431
00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:06.600
We got a fan question about that.
我们收到了一个关于此的粉丝提问。

432
00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:11.080
Olga in Spain said, was it really John or was it a doll?
西班牙的奥尔加问，那是真的约翰还是个玩偶？

433
00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:12.940
Like he, it was John.
那是约翰。

434
00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:13.780
It was John.
那是约翰。

435
00:19:13.900 --> 00:19:17.040
But he fell so convincingly.
但他摔得太逼真了。

436
00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:18.320
It looked like it hurt.
看起来很疼。

437
00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:19.140
It looked perfect.
看起来太完美了。

438
00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:20.220
He went noodle.
他整个人像面条一样瘫下去了。

439
00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:21.200
He did.
确实。

440
00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:23.980
It was very well done.
做得非常好。

441
00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:25.140
It was John.
那是约翰。

442
00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:25.800
Yeah.
是啊。

443
00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:29.240
The episode is going to start now with Jim.
剧集现在要从吉姆开始了。

444
00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:32.020
He's in the lobby gift shop, it looks like, of the hotel.
他看起来是在酒店大堂的礼品店里。

445
00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:32.760
He is.
没错。

446
00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:36.780
And Dwight's trying to get everyone, you know, out the door, into the van.
德怀特正试图让大家出门，上货车。

447
00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:38.420
The scene was much longer.
这场戏原本长得多。

448
00:19:38.540 --> 00:19:39.620
It's in the deleted scenes.
在删减片段里。

449
00:19:40.420 --> 00:19:44.740
Erin actually goes up to Jim and is like, well, what do you like better, stuffed animals or puppets?
艾琳其实走过去问吉姆，你更喜欢毛绒玩具还是木偶？

450
00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:47.800
And Erin has strong opinions about this.
而且艾琳对此有强烈的看法。

451
00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:48.260
Oh.
噢。

452
00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:49.560
Jim was not ready for.
吉姆还没准备好。

453
00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:50.600
Is it puppets?
是木偶吗？

454
00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:54.420
She said puppets because they're stuffed animals that can actually do something.
她说木偶是因为它们是能动起来的毛绒玩具。

455
00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:58.940
I was curious about this Tallahassee gift shop at the hotel.
我对酒店里的那家塔拉哈西礼品店很好奇。

456
00:19:59.160 --> 00:19:59.560
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

457
00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:01.000
I love a gift shop.
我喜欢礼品店。

458
00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:01.800
I know.
我知道。

459
00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:02.520
I love it.
我超爱。

460
00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:03.880
I'm going to bring you back something.
我会给你带礼物的。

461
00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:06.100
If I go somewhere, I'm bringing you back something.
只要我出门，我都会给你带礼物。

462
00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:12.180
This gift shop had mostly alligators, parrot puppets, lollipops, and flip-flops.
那家礼品店里大多是鳄鱼、鹦鹉木偶、棒棒糖和人字拖。

463
00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:12.820
Okay.
好吧。

464
00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:16.760
This made me very curious about what Tallahassee has to offer.
这让我对塔拉哈西到底有什么好玩的非常好奇。

465
00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:20.260
Should I settle in for a Tallahassee breakdown?
我是不是该深入了解一下塔拉哈西了？

466
00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:26.160
I found so many interesting things about Tallahassee that I'm actually going to sprinkle them throughout the episode.
我发现了关于塔拉哈西的很多趣事，我打算在这一集里穿插着讲出来。

