00:26:54.600 --> 00:27:00.140
Stanley would not like Messina and only want solo Loggins, but it really cracked me up.
即斯坦利不喜欢梅西纳，只想要洛金斯个人作品，但这真的把我逗乐了。

618
00:27:00.240 --> 00:27:03.300
You guys, I'm a total dork for little, tiny jokes like that.
伙计们，我就是个会被这种细小笑话戳中笑点的书呆子。

619
00:27:03.300 --> 00:27:08.980
Well, I noticed something about this scene, which is that it was very windy outside.
嗯，我注意到了这一幕的一个细节，那就是外面风很大。

620
00:27:09.300 --> 00:27:10.520
Did you see the wind?
你看到风了吗？

621
00:27:10.920 --> 00:27:11.100
No.
没有。

622
00:27:11.100 --> 00:27:11.780
So windy.
风太大了。

623
00:27:12.120 --> 00:27:16.300
No, I think I was so fixated on that couplet of dialogue.
没有，我想我当时太专注于那两句对白了。

624
00:27:16.600 --> 00:27:21.840
Well, I noticed it because that's kind of unusual for LA, but I thought it really sold it as Florida.
嗯，我注意到了，因为这在洛杉矶很不寻常，但我认为这确实让它看起来很像佛罗里达。

625
00:27:22.240 --> 00:27:22.820
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

626
00:27:23.140 --> 00:27:24.260
Made it look very tropical.
让它看起来很有热带风情。

627
00:27:24.260 --> 00:27:24.840
Yeah.
是啊。

628
00:27:25.420 --> 00:27:29.880
Well, these guys are all going to head to their meeting, and in the meantime, we're going to head to Scranton.
好吧，这些人都要去开会了，与此同时，我们要去斯克兰顿了。

629
00:27:30.620 --> 00:27:34.400
Andy's going to walk out of his office and notice how incredibly quiet it is.
安迪会走出办公室，注意到外面安静得不可思议。

630
00:27:34.600 --> 00:27:35.780
Yeah, Creed likes it.
是啊，克里德很喜欢这样。

631
00:27:35.840 --> 00:27:37.520
He's already written 12 plays.
他已经写了12个剧本了。

632
00:27:37.720 --> 00:27:37.940
Yeah.
是啊。

633
00:27:38.600 --> 00:27:44.180
Can we please, please have an episode somewhere where we just watch one of Creed's plays?
我们能不能求求你们，拍一集让我们看看克里德写的剧本？

634
00:27:44.200 --> 00:27:45.500
Why didn't that exist?
为什么没拍过？

635
00:27:46.080 --> 00:27:48.620
Because it would be utter nonsense.
因为那绝对会是一团糟。

636
00:27:48.980 --> 00:27:49.460
I know.
我知道。

637
00:27:49.800 --> 00:27:51.400
It would make no sense.
那会完全没逻辑。

638
00:27:52.240 --> 00:27:54.840
Pam wonders, wait, why is it so quiet?
帕姆纳闷，等等，为什么这么安静？

639
00:27:54.840 --> 00:27:59.460
She realizes that it's because no one took the phone off voicemail.
她意识到是因为没人把电话从语音留言模式切出来。

640
00:27:59.840 --> 00:28:00.140
Yeah.
是啊。

641
00:28:00.220 --> 00:28:06.500
The phone hasn't been ringing, and as soon as she takes the phone off voicemail, it rings immediately, and now who's going to answer it?
电话一直没响，她刚把语音留言关掉，电话立刻就响了，现在谁去接呢？

642
00:28:06.700 --> 00:28:13.140
All of a sudden, there's this front reception standoff between Andy and Pam, and Kelly's freaking out.
突然之间，前台陷入了安迪和帕姆的对峙，凯莉快疯了。

643
00:28:13.260 --> 00:28:14.540
She's like, someone just answer it.
她一直在喊，快去接电话啊。

644
00:28:14.540 --> 00:28:16.200
Neither of them want to budge.
他们两个谁都不肯让步。

645
00:28:16.380 --> 00:28:20.360
There was a Pam-deleted talking head that would have gone here, and I want to read it to you.
这里原本有一段帕姆被删减的采访，我想读给你听。

646
00:28:20.440 --> 00:28:20.780
Please.
请读吧。

647
00:28:21.140 --> 00:28:22.160
I remember it.
我记得这段。

648
00:28:22.620 --> 00:28:23.740
Here's what Pam said.
帕姆是这么说的。

649
00:28:24.080 --> 00:28:26.080
I just got back from maternity leave.
我刚休完产假回来。

650
00:28:26.160 --> 00:28:28.340
I can't let them make me the receptioniSt.
我不能让他们让我去当前台。

651
00:28:28.500 --> 00:28:34.020
I've worked way too hard for way too long to get to this place of them thinking I'm the office administrator.
我辛辛苦苦工作了这么久，才走到今天这一步，结果他们还以为我是办公室行政人员。

652
00:28:34.280 --> 00:28:34.680
Yes.
没错。

653
00:28:35.980 --> 00:28:39.020
We got a piece of mail about this scene from Charlotte E.
我们收到了一封关于这个场景的邮件，来自加拿大的夏洛特·E。

654
00:28:39.120 --> 00:28:41.220
in Canada, but who is living in the U.K.
但她现在住在英国。

655
00:28:42.200 --> 00:28:49.660
Charlotte said, I just want to say how much I appreciate the scene where Pam does not pick up the phone in the end, because that's not her job anymore.
夏洛特说，我只想说，我非常欣赏帕姆最后没有接电话的那一幕，因为那已经不是她的工作了。

656
00:28:50.000 --> 00:28:59.660
There's so much underlying expectations sometimes in an office environment, and as someone who moved from a support team role to a non-support team role in my current job,
在办公室环境中，有时会有很多潜在的期望，作为一个在目前的工作中从支持团队转到非支持团队的人，

657
00:28:59.660 --> 00:29:08.160
you've got to stand your ground and kindly redirect people to the right person when they look to you to buy milk or find a power cord.
你必须坚持自己的立场，当别人指望你去买牛奶或找电源线时，要礼貌地引导他们去找正确的人。

658
00:29:08.300 --> 00:29:10.240
Those were very specific examples, Charlotte.
这些例子非常具体，夏洛特。

659
00:29:10.660 --> 00:29:12.360
Anyway, Charlotte goes on to say,
总之，夏洛特接着说，

660
00:29:12.360 --> 00:29:19.320
it's not about not being a team player, but about the subtle implication that their time is more important than my time,
这并不是说不合群，而是因为这其中有一种微妙的暗示，即他们的时间比我的时间更重要，

661
00:29:19.460 --> 00:29:22.780
just because you once took care of those housekeeping things.
仅仅因为你曾经负责过那些杂务。

662
00:29:23.100 --> 00:29:28.980
Anyway, I was just willing Pam not to pick up the phone, and I'm so glad when she didn't.
总之，我当时一直在心里祈祷帕姆不要接电话，她没接我真是太高兴了。

663
00:29:29.620 --> 00:29:33.280
Well, Charlotte, I also like that Pam stood her ground for all these reasons.
嗯，夏洛特，我也很欣赏帕姆出于这些原因坚持自己的立场。

664
00:29:33.280 --> 00:29:42.140
However, it does feel like reception is maybe part of Pam's quote-unquote department,
不过，前台似乎确实属于帕姆所谓的“部门”，

665
00:29:42.140 --> 00:29:48.380
and with both the temp and the receptionist gone, it feels like she's the last person left in that department
而且临时工和前台都不在，感觉她是那个部门剩下的最后一个人，

666
00:29:48.380 --> 00:29:51.020
and maybe, probably, maybe should have answered the phone.
所以也许、大概、可能还是应该接一下电话的。

667
00:29:51.700 --> 00:29:53.780
I mean, yes.
我是说，是的。

668
00:29:54.180 --> 00:29:54.820
Yes.
没错。

669
00:29:55.020 --> 00:29:56.400
I think so.
我也这么认为。

670
00:29:56.400 --> 00:30:02.340
I support Pam's stance of not answering the phones because it will set a precedent.
我支持帕姆不接电话的立场，因为这会立下一个先例。

671
00:30:02.660 --> 00:30:04.680
But yeah, it is her department.
但确实，那属于她的部门。

672
00:30:05.080 --> 00:30:10.620
And if she's not going to answer the phone, I believe she's responsible for finding someone to answer the phone.
如果她不打算接电话，我认为她有责任找别人来接。

673
00:30:10.820 --> 00:30:11.440
There it is.
就是这样。

674
00:30:11.520 --> 00:30:11.760
Right?
对吧？

675
00:30:11.980 --> 00:30:12.280
Yes.
是的。

676
00:30:12.920 --> 00:30:17.140
Next up, Jim tells Kathy that Stanley drives fast,
接下来，吉姆告诉凯西斯坦利开车很快，

677
00:30:17.340 --> 00:30:20.800
and Stanley explains that life is short, and one of his mottos is,
斯坦利解释说人生苦短，他的座右铭之一是，

678
00:30:20.920 --> 00:30:22.880
drive fast, leave a sexy corpse.
开车要快，留下一具性感的尸体。

679
00:30:23.820 --> 00:30:25.700
We had a fan question from Charlotte M.
我们收到了来自华盛顿特区的夏洛特·M的粉丝提问，她说，

680
00:30:25.720 --> 00:30:27.240
in Washington, D.C., who said,
我等了很久才发来这个问题。

681
00:30:27.420 --> 00:30:29.760
I have been waiting for so long to send in this question.
这是我在整部剧中，斯坦利最棒的一句台词。

682
00:30:30.060 --> 00:30:32.920
This is my top Stanley line in the whole series.
当时有备选台词吗？

683
00:30:32.920 --> 00:30:35.000
Were there any candy bag alts?
我去查了备选台词库。

684
00:30:35.800 --> 00:30:37.220
I went to the candy bag.
我也查了。

685
00:30:37.420 --> 00:30:38.160
I did, too.
我没看到任何备选。

686
00:30:38.460 --> 00:30:39.620
I didn't see any.
没有备选。

687
00:30:39.740 --> 00:30:40.540
No alts.
这句台词的剧本写得和他说的完全一样。

688
00:30:40.700 --> 00:30:43.420
And this line was scripted exactly the way he said it.
是的。

689
00:30:43.520 --> 00:30:43.800
Yes.
但这确实让我很想知道斯坦利还有没有其他的座右铭。

690
00:30:44.480 --> 00:30:48.300
But it did make me want to know if Stanley had any other mottos.
我真希望编剧们有一张斯坦利座右铭的草稿清单。

691
00:30:48.300 --> 00:30:53.800
I wish that there was, like, just a writer's pitch sheet of Stanley mottos.
我相信那东西肯定存在于某个地方。

692
00:30:54.280 --> 00:30:55.880
I'm sure it exists somewhere.
我其实正想问你关于剧集设定集的事，看看里面有没有提到。

693
00:30:55.880 --> 00:30:59.940
I was actually going to ask you about the show Bible, if it said anything in the show Bible.
如果有一页叫“斯坦利的座右铭”，但我相信是没有的。

694
00:31:00.220 --> 00:31:03.860
If there was a page called Stanley's Mottos, I believe there is not.
我真希望有。

695
00:31:04.500 --> 00:31:05.960
I wish there was.
猜猜还有谁在这个会议上？

696
00:31:06.580 --> 00:31:08.420
Guess who else is at this conference?
吃豆人回来了。

697
00:31:08.960 --> 00:31:10.560
The Pac-Man is back.
吉姆和德怀特曾试图让他被解雇，但他却在佛罗里达站稳了脚跟。

698
00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:14.320
Jim and Dwight tried to get him fired, but he landed on his feet in Florida.
是啊，他有九条命，还有九英寸。

699
00:31:14.320 --> 00:31:16.800
Yeah, he's got nine lives and a nine-inch.
九英寸的其他东西。

700
00:31:17.220 --> 00:31:18.680
Nine inches of other things.
九英寸的其他东西。

701
00:31:18.880 --> 00:31:19.060
Yep.
没错。

702
00:31:19.220 --> 00:31:19.460
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

703
00:31:20.300 --> 00:31:26.920
Now we get to introduce Nellie Bertram, one of my favorite introductions ever.
现在我们要介绍奈莉·伯特拉姆了，这是我最喜欢的出场方式之一。

704
00:31:27.260 --> 00:31:31.340
I love how she just selects Ryan and just starts whispering to him.
我喜欢她直接挑中瑞安，然后开始对他耳语。

705
00:31:31.440 --> 00:31:33.040
And also, Ryan doesn't question it.
而且，瑞安竟然一点也不质疑。

706
00:31:33.200 --> 00:31:33.420
I know.
我知道。

707
00:31:33.420 --> 00:31:35.800
He just starts saying what she's telling him to say.
他直接开始复述她让他说的话。

708
00:31:35.960 --> 00:31:36.360
Yes.
是的。

709
00:31:36.360 --> 00:31:38.160
What does she get Ryan to say?
她让瑞安说了什么？

710
00:31:38.160 --> 00:31:43.020
She says, psst, say, so who's leading this thing anyway?
她说，嘘，说，到底是谁在领导这事儿？

711
00:31:44.860 --> 00:31:46.920
Psst, say, I can't wait to meet him.
嘘，说，我等不及要见他了。

712
00:31:47.720 --> 00:31:48.120
Yes.
没错。

713
00:31:48.380 --> 00:31:50.720
And then she stands up and says, him, you say?
然后她站起来说，你说“他”？

714
00:31:50.880 --> 00:31:52.240
Don't think a woman could be a leader?
觉得女人当不了领导？

715
00:31:52.560 --> 00:31:54.220
You poor simple boy.
你这可怜又单纯的男孩。

716
00:31:55.320 --> 00:31:55.840
Yes.
没错。

717
00:31:56.000 --> 00:31:57.700
And then she launches into a speech.
接着她就开始了一段演讲。

718
00:31:57.700 --> 00:32:06.020
And I want to ask you, Angela, if I'm ever asked to do like a commencement speech at my college or a college,
安吉拉，我想问你，如果我以后受邀去我的母校或者其他大学做毕业演讲，

719
00:32:06.220 --> 00:32:09.000
can I start my speech like this?
我能这样开场吗？

720
00:32:09.480 --> 00:32:10.580
Can I do this?
我能这么做吗？

721
00:32:11.340 --> 00:32:13.020
Expected a man, did you?
以为是个男人，对吧？

722
00:32:13.680 --> 00:32:16.360
Strong, powerful, huge, whopping penis?
强壮、有力、巨大、硕大的阴茎？

723
00:32:16.740 --> 00:32:20.940
Well, sorry to disappoint, but my huge, whopping penis is right here.
抱歉让你们失望了，但我那硕大的阴茎就在这儿。

724
00:32:21.100 --> 00:32:22.520
Then I point to my brain.
然后我指着我的大脑。

725
00:32:22.720 --> 00:32:24.620
And I'm not afraid to use it.
而且我敢于使用它。

726
00:32:24.740 --> 00:32:28.100
So stop looking at my breasts and start looking at my penis.
所以别盯着我的胸部看，开始盯着我的阴茎看吧。

727
00:32:29.120 --> 00:32:30.720
Can I start it that way?
我能那样开场吗？

728
00:32:30.860 --> 00:32:32.100
Will people get it?
人们会懂吗？

729
00:32:34.240 --> 00:32:35.620
That would be amazing.
那一定会很棒。

730
00:32:35.900 --> 00:32:36.500
Can I?
我可以吗？

731
00:32:36.660 --> 00:32:37.840
I really want to know.
我真的很想知道。

732
00:32:37.980 --> 00:32:38.860
I want you to do it.
我希望你这么做。

733
00:32:39.500 --> 00:32:45.220
There is going to be an event, and I'm going to start it that way, and we'll see how it goes.
以后肯定会有个活动，我就要那样开场，看看效果如何。

734
00:32:45.720 --> 00:32:49.740
There's going to be a whole ton of people that don't get it and think you've lost it.
肯定会有一大堆人听不懂，觉得你疯了。

735
00:32:49.760 --> 00:32:50.140
I know.
我知道。

736
00:32:50.300 --> 00:32:53.320
And then there'll be like a few people in the corner that are like, woohoo!
然后角落里会有几个人欢呼，喔吼！

737
00:32:54.580 --> 00:32:56.120
Season eight, tell us.
第八季，告诉我们吧。

738
00:32:57.960 --> 00:33:00.400
So Nellie, yes, is now running the meeting.
所以奈莉，没错，现在由她主持会议。

739
00:33:00.640 --> 00:33:07.760
She's going to explain the origin of this project, which is that she interviewed to be the potential branch manager in Scranton.
她要解释这个项目的由来，也就是她曾面试过斯克兰顿分公司的经理职位。

740
00:33:07.900 --> 00:33:11.060
She points right at Jim and says, but I didn't get the job.
她直接指着吉姆说，但我没得到那份工作。

741
00:33:11.980 --> 00:33:15.640
And apparently she got really upset about this and went on a shopping spree.
显然她为此非常难过，于是去疯狂购物了一番。

742
00:33:15.960 --> 00:33:17.900
She bought 13 pianos.
她买了13架钢琴。

743
00:33:17.900 --> 00:33:19.320
So all of this,
所以这一切，

744
00:33:19.440 --> 00:33:30.100
when she's explaining her breakdown and how she bought the pianos and then how she had this epiphany about selling things and she went and talked to Joe and then she got the job.
当她解释自己的崩溃，解释她如何买下那些钢琴，如何对销售产生顿悟，然后去找乔谈话，最后得到了这份工作时。

745
00:33:30.260 --> 00:33:38.480
It was so well done that I went to the script because I wanted to know like how much of it was scripted and maybe did Catherine improvise.
演得太好了，我特意去看了剧本，因为我想知道有多少是写好的，凯瑟琳是不是即兴发挥了。

746
00:33:38.480 --> 00:33:41.520
Because it was scripted word for word.
因为剧本里就是逐字逐句写好的。

747
00:33:41.680 --> 00:33:43.320
That is how good she is.
这就是她有多厉害。

748
00:33:43.680 --> 00:33:47.080
I thought she was literally coming up with half that stuff on the fly.
我原以为她有一半内容是现场发挥的。

749
00:33:47.280 --> 00:33:53.540
That just shows, I feel like, when we have good writing and then a great performer, how just magic.
我觉得这正说明了，当有好剧本加上优秀的演员时，效果是多么神奇。

750
00:33:54.140 --> 00:33:57.800
Watching Catherine in this scene, I totally lost where I was.
看着凯瑟琳演这一幕，我完全忘了自己身在何处。

751
00:33:58.000 --> 00:33:58.360
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

752
00:33:58.660 --> 00:34:05.580
And if I had been in that conference room, I would have forgotten to act because I was just so enthralled with her performance.
如果当时我在那个会议室里，我肯定会忘了要演戏，因为我完全被她的表演迷住了。

753
00:34:05.580 --> 00:34:08.820
I wish it would have gone on another five minutes.
真希望那段表演能再多持续五分钟。

754
00:34:08.860 --> 00:34:11.260
Like, I could have watched even more of that.
我是说，我真想再多看一会儿。

755
00:34:11.760 --> 00:34:19.240
Well, lady, I think we should take a break before we get too deep into Dwight's appendicitis and Andy's obsession with reception.
好吧，女士，我觉得在深入讨论德怀特的阑尾炎和安迪对前台的痴迷之前，我们应该先休息一下。

756
00:34:19.500 --> 00:34:19.900
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

757
00:34:20.040 --> 00:34:27.100
And when we come back, I actually have some interesting details on how this episode was received by fans and critics.
等我们回来，我其实还有些有趣的细节要分享，关于这一集在粉丝和评论家中的反响。

758
00:34:27.340 --> 00:34:28.980
There was a lot of hubba-bub.
当时引起了不小的轰动。

759
00:34:29.400 --> 00:34:31.100
Did Miles McNutt write about it?
迈尔斯·麦克纳特写过相关的评论吗？

760
00:34:31.280 --> 00:34:33.400
He did, and I'm going to tell you what he said.
他写了，我正要告诉你他说了什么。

761
00:34:33.660 --> 00:34:33.960
Okay.
好的。

762
00:34:33.960 --> 00:34:45.700
All right, we are back.
好了，我们回来了。

763
00:34:46.160 --> 00:34:54.140
And before we keep breaking down this episode, I thought maybe you might be interested to know how this episode, Tallahassee, was received.
在继续剖析这一集之前，我想你可能想知道这一集《塔拉哈西》的反响如何。

764
00:34:54.380 --> 00:34:55.680
I am so interested.
我太想知道了。

765
00:34:56.100 --> 00:34:56.720
All right.
好的。

766
00:34:57.020 --> 00:34:58.420
It was very mixed.
评价非常两极分化。

767
00:34:58.660 --> 00:34:59.000
Hmm.
嗯。

768
00:34:59.240 --> 00:35:04.260
But it was sort of everybody versus Miles McNutt.
但基本上是所有人都在反对迈尔斯·麦克纳特。

769
00:35:04.620 --> 00:35:05.080
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

770
00:35:05.080 --> 00:35:15.620
Okay, so TVEquals did a review of this episode and said it was one of the best episodes of the season and maybe even of the last couple of seasons.
是这样，TVEquals网站对这一集做了评论，称其为本季最棒的剧集之一，甚至可能是过去几季里最好的。

771
00:35:15.900 --> 00:35:16.160
Wow.
哇。

772
00:35:16.160 --> 00:35:27.340
Among Office Tally fans, Tallahassee was ranked number one for season eight, the number one episode, most favorite among fans on Office Tally.
在Office Tally的粉丝中，《塔拉哈西》被评为第八季的第一名，是粉丝们最喜欢的一集。

773
00:35:27.520 --> 00:35:28.960
Of all of season eight?
整个第八季的第一名？

774
00:35:29.060 --> 00:35:30.160
Of all of season eight.
整个第八季的第一名。

775
00:35:31.200 --> 00:35:34.840
However, Miles McNutt, not a fan.
然而，迈尔斯·麦克纳特并不喜欢。

776
00:35:35.620 --> 00:35:36.840
Gave it a C minus.
他给了个C减。

777
00:35:37.280 --> 00:35:37.540
Hmm.
嗯。

778
00:35:38.700 --> 00:35:39.640
Here's a quote.
这是他的一段引语。

779
00:35:40.740 --> 00:35:46.580
While I left last week's episode with a sense of hope, Tallahassee has lived up to none of that potential.
虽然上周的那一集让我感到了一丝希望，但《塔拉哈西》完全没有达到那种潜力。

780
00:35:46.840 --> 00:35:47.660
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

781
00:35:49.800 --> 00:35:52.900
And you can imagine the rest of the review from there.
你可以想象剩下的评论内容了。

782
00:35:53.040 --> 00:35:53.160
Yeah.
是啊。

783
00:35:53.820 --> 00:35:55.480
Well, he got some pushback.
不过，他确实遭到了一些反击。

784
00:35:55.920 --> 00:35:57.840
A fan named Steve B.
一位名叫史蒂夫·B的粉丝

785
00:35:58.020 --> 00:36:00.500
wrote on the comment board, quote,
在评论区写道，引用如下：

786
00:36:00.720 --> 00:36:04.100
I think you need to recuse yourself from reviewing this show.
我觉得你需要回避对这部剧的评论工作。

787
00:36:04.560 --> 00:36:07.820
Each week, you find a new reason to hate a particular episode.
每周你都能找到新的理由去讨厌某一集。

788
00:36:08.080 --> 00:36:11.500
When the show gives you what you want, you find another reason.
当剧集给了你想要的东西时，你又会找别的理由。

789
00:36:11.760 --> 00:36:17.200
For the last two seasons, you've been hitting the drumbeat of character-based comedy pretty hard.
过去两季里，你一直都在极力鼓吹以角色为基础的喜剧。

790
00:36:17.200 --> 00:36:26.180
Yet, here we have an episode that hinges largely on Dwight's characterization, his belligerence, ambition, paranoia, and contempt for the common man.
然而，这一集很大程度上正是基于德怀特的性格刻画——他的好斗、野心、偏执以及对普通人的蔑视。

791
00:36:26.340 --> 00:36:28.280
And it was a funny episode.
而且这确实是一集很有趣的剧集。

792
00:36:28.660 --> 00:36:29.820
Well, guess what?
嗯，你猜怎么着？

793
00:36:30.040 --> 00:36:30.380
What?
什么？

794
00:36:30.760 --> 00:36:36.520
In his review for After Hours, which is next week's episode, Miles McNutt said this.
在他对下一集《下班后》的评论中，迈尔斯·麦克纳特说了这样的话。

795
00:36:36.800 --> 00:36:38.940
Did he address Steve B.?
他回应史蒂夫·B了吗？

796
00:36:38.940 --> 00:36:41.560
Well, sort of.
算是吧。

797
00:36:42.280 --> 00:36:43.600
Miles said, quote,
迈尔斯说，引用如下：

798
00:36:43.600 --> 00:36:48.060
Last week's episode probably should have been above a C-minus.
上周的那一集评分或许应该高于C减。

799
00:36:48.240 --> 00:36:48.500
Oh.
哦。

800
00:36:48.780 --> 00:36:51.600
But I went with my gut, and I have to stand by that decision.
但我当时是凭直觉给出的评价，我必须坚持那个决定。

801
00:36:51.960 --> 00:36:52.860
Go Miles.
迈尔斯上吧。

802
00:36:53.180 --> 00:36:56.380
I support him standing by his first reaction.
我支持他坚持自己的第一反应。

803
00:36:56.700 --> 00:36:58.260
Yes, that was his first reaction.
没错，那就是他的第一反应。

804
00:36:58.780 --> 00:37:06.380
I'll tell you, among fans, generally they loved this episode, but the cold open was hotly debated.
我跟你说，粉丝们总体上很喜欢这一集，但开场戏引发了激烈的争论。

805
00:37:06.380 --> 00:37:09.640
There was a huge lover hate of the cold open.
大家对这段开场戏的态度两极分化非常严重。

806
00:37:10.100 --> 00:37:12.140
We got a letter from Dennis D.
我们收到了一封来自丹尼斯·D的信，

807
00:37:12.360 --> 00:37:15.060
in Tallahassee, Florida, who said,
他来自佛罗里达州的塔拉哈西，他说，

808
00:37:15.240 --> 00:37:19.740
My favorite prank in the show is this episode's cold open.
我最喜欢的整蛊桥段就是这一集的开场戏。

809
00:37:20.020 --> 00:37:23.980
But the message boards regarding this cold open, when the show aired,
但在节目播出时，关于这段开场戏的留言板上，

810
00:37:24.120 --> 00:37:30.640
one person said they deleted the episode from their DVR after watching the cold open because they hated it so much.
有人说他们在看完开场戏后就把录像机里的这一集删了，因为他们太讨厌了。

811
00:37:30.980 --> 00:37:31.120
Wow.
哇。

812
00:37:31.120 --> 00:37:34.880
But then other people said it was the funniest cold open in a long time.
但也有人说这是很久以来最搞笑的开场戏。

813
00:37:35.040 --> 00:37:35.920
They agreed with Dennis.
他们和丹尼斯的观点一致。

814
00:37:36.020 --> 00:37:37.300
You can't make everybody happy.
你不可能让所有人都满意。

815
00:37:37.440 --> 00:37:37.940
You can't.
确实不能。

816
00:37:38.060 --> 00:37:41.180
You especially can't make Miles McNutt happy very easily.
尤其是想让迈尔斯·麦克纳特满意，可没那么容易。

817
00:37:41.440 --> 00:37:46.000
I have to wonder, and I'm sure it's not, is Steve B.
我不得不怀疑，虽然肯定不是，那个史蒂夫·B是不是……

818
00:37:46.160 --> 00:37:47.300
Steve Burgess?
史蒂夫·伯吉斯？

819
00:37:48.180 --> 00:37:48.740
Wait.
等等。

820
00:37:49.800 --> 00:37:50.360
Wait.
等等。

821
00:37:50.640 --> 00:37:52.120
That is so funny.
那太搞笑了。

822
00:37:52.300 --> 00:37:55.060
Did Steve Burgess go on Miles McNutt's review?
史蒂夫·伯吉斯去迈尔斯·麦克纳特的评论区留言了吗？

823
00:37:55.360 --> 00:37:59.400
I'm sure he did it because he's busy and he probably never would have done that.
我肯定他没去，因为他很忙，而且他可能根本不会做那种事。

824
00:37:59.400 --> 00:38:02.700
But it is kind of funny that it's Steve B.
但那个史蒂夫·B确实挺搞笑的。

825
00:38:03.060 --> 00:38:04.940
I didn't even think of that, Angela.
安吉拉，我甚至都没往那儿想。

826
00:38:05.180 --> 00:38:06.700
I kind of want to ask Steve.
我真想去问问史蒂夫。

827
00:38:06.840 --> 00:38:07.340
I know.
我知道。

828
00:38:07.540 --> 00:38:08.000
I do, too.
我也想。

829
00:38:08.160 --> 00:38:11.440
Did you ever write on Miles McNutt's comment board?
你有没有在迈尔斯·麦克纳特的评论区写过留言？

830
00:38:11.960 --> 00:38:13.620
Oh, I love that so much.
哦，我太喜欢这个主意了。

831
00:38:13.620 --> 00:38:16.160
And ask him to recuse himself.
然后要求他回避。

832
00:38:19.060 --> 00:38:24.840
Well, I want to point out this next scene because, you know, Dwight is really popping the antacids now.
好吧，我想指出接下来的这一幕，因为你知道，德怀特现在真的在狂吃抗酸药了。

833
00:38:25.000 --> 00:38:26.300
He's in major pain.
他正处于剧痛之中。

834
00:38:26.380 --> 00:38:26.880
He is.
确实如此。

835
00:38:26.880 --> 00:38:31.460
And Nellie is going to ask someone to help with the projection screen to pull it down.
奈莉打算找人帮忙把投影幕拉下来。

836
00:38:31.640 --> 00:38:33.680
She points out that Ryan couldn't reach it.
她指出瑞安够不着。

837
00:38:33.820 --> 00:38:35.440
It would be so funny if he tried.
如果他试着去拉，那肯定会很搞笑。

838
00:38:35.580 --> 00:38:36.280
My balloon.
我的气球。

839
00:38:38.360 --> 00:38:43.900
And it's in this moment that Dwight's like, I must appear like a strong, tall leader.
就在那一刻，德怀特心想，我必须表现得像个强壮、高大的领导者。

840
00:38:44.200 --> 00:38:46.260
Especially because she asked Jim to do it, right?
尤其是因为她让吉姆去拉，对吧？

841
00:38:46.260 --> 00:38:52.420
I have to say, Rainn Wilson completely crushed it.
我不得不说，雷恩·威尔森演得太棒了。

842
00:38:52.620 --> 00:38:57.580
The way he sold his pain as he reaches up for that screen to pull it down.
他伸手去拉屏幕时表现出的那种痛苦感，演得太真实了。

843
00:38:58.360 --> 00:39:00.680
I thought he was brilliant in this whole episode.
我觉得他在这一整集里的表现都非常出色。

844
00:39:00.980 --> 00:39:03.680
The way he portrayed his pain escalating.
他演绎痛苦逐渐加剧的方式太绝了。

845
00:39:03.980 --> 00:39:06.340
I honestly, Rainn, oh my God.
说真的，雷恩，天哪。

846
00:39:06.520 --> 00:39:08.300
You were so great in this episode.
你在这一集里表现得太棒了。

847
00:39:08.780 --> 00:39:10.900
I thought you should have won an Emmy for playing Dwight.
我觉得你本该凭德怀特这个角色拿艾美奖的。

848
00:39:11.060 --> 00:39:12.560
He was nominated three times.
他被提名过三次。

849
00:39:12.860 --> 00:39:14.100
You and John were nominated.
你和约翰都获得过提名。

850
00:39:14.400 --> 00:39:16.460
Steve, none of you guys won an Emmy.
史蒂夫，你们谁都没拿过艾美奖。

851
00:39:16.700 --> 00:39:18.260
You all should have won Emmys.
你们都该拿艾美奖的。

852
00:39:18.480 --> 00:39:18.920
Wow.
哇。

853
00:39:19.100 --> 00:39:20.580
This has taken a turn.
事情变得有点不一样了。

854
00:39:20.580 --> 00:39:21.320
This speech.
这段发言。

855
00:39:21.480 --> 00:39:25.220
It's turned into a We Deserve Emmys speech because of the pulling down of the screen.
因为那个投影幕被拉下来，这变成了一段“我们理应拿艾美奖”的发言。

856
00:39:25.460 --> 00:39:25.960
I love it.
我喜欢。

857
00:39:25.960 --> 00:39:27.200
So many other moments.
还有好多其他瞬间。

858
00:39:27.360 --> 00:39:31.620
And you know, you were sitting right by me when Steve didn't win and it was his last
你知道吗，史蒂夫没获奖时你就坐在我旁边，那可是他最后一次获得提名，

859
00:39:31.620 --> 00:39:34.680
time nominated and I couldn't control myself and I said a curse word.
我当时控制不住自己，还骂了句脏话。

860
00:39:34.760 --> 00:39:35.240
You did.
你确实骂了。

861
00:39:35.420 --> 00:39:36.480
With the camera right by me.
摄像机当时就在我旁边。

862
00:39:36.580 --> 00:39:36.740
Yeah.
是啊。

863
00:39:37.960 --> 00:39:40.420
I just thought Rainn should have won an Emmy.
我只是觉得雷恩应该拿个艾美奖。

864
00:39:40.760 --> 00:39:43.280
Well, you know who agrees with you is Kelly M.
好吧，你知道谁同意你的观点吗？是来自弗吉尼亚州伍德布里奇的凯莉·M。

865
00:39:43.480 --> 00:39:44.940
from Woodbridge, Virginia.
凯莉安写信来说，我等了很久才给你们几位女士投这个稿。

866
00:39:45.860 --> 00:39:50.920
Kellyanne wrote in and said, I have been waiting for so long to submit this to you ladies.
我想帮你们省点深入挖掘的时间。

867
00:39:51.600 --> 00:39:54.220
I thought I would save you some time on a deep dive.
我是一名明尼苏达州的儿科注册护士，几乎每个班次都要接触阑尾炎患儿。

868
00:39:54.220 --> 00:40:00.500
I am a pediatric RN in Minnesota and I work with kids with appendicitis nearly every shift.
我自己也切除过阑尾。

869
00:40:00.500 --> 00:40:02.800
I have also had my own appendix removed.
哦，哇。

870
00:40:03.040 --> 00:40:03.400
Oh, wow.
最明显的症状是，当我们医护人员轻轻按压某人的腹部时，

871
00:40:03.600 --> 00:40:09.440
The most distinct symptom is when we as medical personnel push slightly on someone's abdomen
最痛的时候其实是松开压力的时候，而不是施加压力的时候。

872
00:40:09.440 --> 00:40:14.700
and the most pain is actually when we release the pressure, not when we apply the pressure.
我们称之为反跳痛。

873
00:40:14.900 --> 00:40:17.140
We call this rebound tenderness.
阑尾炎是一个严重的医疗问题，这一集中有几个瞬间让我印象深刻，

874
00:40:18.060 --> 00:40:22.880
Appendicitis is a serious medical issue and there were a few moments that stuck out to me in this
展现了雷恩·威尔森的演技有多出色。

875
00:40:22.880 --> 00:40:25.880
episode that shows how well Rainn Wilson performed.
首先是他整集走路和站立的姿势。

876
00:40:26.500 --> 00:40:29.540
First is the way he walks and stands through the whole episode.
他一走出酒店，我看到抗酸药和那副佝偻着走路的样子，我就有种预感是阑尾炎。

877
00:40:29.700 --> 00:40:34.900
As soon as he walked out of the hotel, I saw the antacids and the hunched over walk and I had a
当他伸手去拉投影幕时，那样子既让人难受又很好笑，因为我太清楚那种感觉了，

878
00:40:34.900 --> 00:40:36.060
feeling it was appendicitis.
因为患阑尾炎时站直身体会非常疼。

879
00:40:36.560 --> 00:40:41.560
When he reached for the projector screen, it was so uncomfortable but also so funny because I knew
然后，当然，他继续表现出更多的症状和更剧烈的疼痛。

880
00:40:41.560 --> 00:40:47.380
exactly how that felt because standing up straight hurts so bad when you have appendicitis.
我必须给雷恩·威尔森的精准表演点个大大的赞。

881
00:40:47.380 --> 00:40:51.720
And then, of course, he goes on to show more symptoms and more severe pain.
简直太真实了。

882
00:40:51.940 --> 00:40:55.740
I have to give huge props to Rainn Wilson for his spot-on performance.
他整集中症状的逐渐演变非常完美，我享受其中的每一分钟。

883
00:40:55.740 --> 00:40:57.320
It was just so believable.
另外，也要为丹尼尔·春和编剧团队鼓掌，他们做了功课，让这一切如此逼真。

884
00:40:57.740 --> 00:41:03.020
His gradual progression of symptoms throughout the episode is perfect and I loved every minute of it.
凯莉安，谢谢你写信来。

885
00:41:03.460 --> 00:41:08.960
Also, applause to Daniel Chun and the writing staff for doing their research to make this so realistic.
你显然是阑尾炎方面的专家，我很高兴我们能把它刻画得这么好。

886
00:41:09.560 --> 00:41:11.240
Kellyanne, thank you for writing in.
我也是！

887
00:41:11.400 --> 00:41:16.360
You're clearly an expert on appendicitis and I'm so glad we did a good portrayal of this.
从剧本到雷恩的表演，那确实值得一座艾美奖。

888
00:41:16.360 --> 00:41:17.200
Me too!
没错。

889
00:41:17.500 --> 00:41:21.740
From the writing to Rainn's performance, which deserved an Emmy.
德怀特终于忍无可忍，他打了电话，我猜是打给911？

890
00:41:22.020 --> 00:41:22.280
Yes.
我不知道他打给了谁。

891
00:41:22.880 --> 00:41:26.920
Dwight has finally had enough with the pain and he has called, I guess, 911?
他打给了某个医疗专业人士，说他出现的症状可能像是中毒或阑尾炎。

892
00:41:27.720 --> 00:41:29.080
I don't know who he's called.
吉姆说，德怀特，我没给你下毒。

893
00:41:29.220 --> 00:41:36.560
He's called someone in the medical profession and he's saying he has symptoms that might mimic being poisoned or appendicitis.
是啊。

894
00:41:37.020 --> 00:41:38.760
Jim's like, Dwight, I didn't poison you.
然后德怀特就说，快给我叫救护车。

895
00:41:39.020 --> 00:41:39.360
Yeah.
直到他发现奈莉需要一个特别项目副总裁，然后他就挂断了电话。

896
00:41:39.840 --> 00:41:42.420
And that's when Dwight's like, get me an ambulance right away.
是啊。

897
00:41:42.420 --> 00:41:50.320
Until he discovers that Nellie needs someone in the position of vice president of special projects and then he gets off the phone.
德怀特有一句口头禅，我现在打算把它用到我的生活中，以后只要我想说，特别是心烦意乱的时候，我就会说出来。

898
00:41:50.820 --> 00:41:50.960
Yeah.
是什么？

899
00:41:51.240 --> 00:41:58.540
Dwight has a phrase I am now going to adopt into my life and I'm going to say it whenever I want, especially if I'm agitated.
你们都该拿艾美奖的。

900
00:41:58.800 --> 00:41:59.560
What is it?
哇。

901
00:41:59.780 --> 00:42:01.820
Send it to the freaking moon, idiot.
把它送去该死的月球吧，白痴。

902
00:42:02.380 --> 00:42:02.860
Okay.
好的。

903
